WEBVTT

1
00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:10.334
After twenty days of continuous bombing,
Nanking finally fell to the Japanese.

2
00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:13.043
It was December the 13th, 1937.

3
00:02:13.584 --> 00:02:16.376
I remember
everyone was running that day,

4
00:02:16.543 --> 00:02:18.909
but no one could escape that heavy fog.

5
00:02:24.026 --> 00:02:25.884
Major Li only had a few men left.

6
00:02:25.893 --> 00:02:28.459
Nanking was no longer
able to put up a fight,

7
00:02:28.793 --> 00:02:31.551
and those left behind,
ran for their lives.

8
00:02:59.101 --> 00:03:02.368
Stop counting.
Shu and two others are missing.

9
00:03:40.293 --> 00:03:41.793
Let us in!

10
00:03:41.959 --> 00:03:43.418
There's no room!

11
00:03:43.584 --> 00:03:45.501
Find your own place to hide!

12
00:03:46.293 --> 00:03:48.334
I said, there's no more room!

13
00:03:48.768 --> 00:03:50.193
Let's go.

14
00:04:02.793 --> 00:04:04.334
Keep going!

15
00:04:15.876 --> 00:04:17.101
Hey.

16
00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:22.318
- There are people inside.
- Who is there?

17
00:04:22.409 --> 00:04:23.676
Come out!

18
00:04:24.834 --> 00:04:26.126
Come out!

19
00:04:31.459 --> 00:04:32.751
Bastards!

20
00:04:34.418 --> 00:04:36.059
Go to hell!

21
00:05:33.476 --> 00:05:34.584
Stop!

22
00:05:36.559 --> 00:05:37.968
Turn around!

23
00:05:43.351 --> 00:05:44.801
Turn around!

24
00:05:50.501 --> 00:05:51.926
Don't move!

25
00:05:52.126 --> 00:05:54.201
American, I'm a refuge.

26
00:05:54.251 --> 00:05:56.193
- What?
- American.

27
00:05:56.959 --> 00:05:58.493
Not soldier.

28
00:06:04.459 --> 00:06:06.676
- John Miller.
- Raise your hands!

29
00:06:06.834 --> 00:06:09.518
- Working at the church.
- Raise your hands!

30
00:06:11.476 --> 00:06:13.526
I said raise your hands!

31
00:06:44.834 --> 00:06:46.201
Separated...

32
00:06:46.918 --> 00:06:49.876
You separated from your families?

33
00:06:51.351 --> 00:06:53.459
Uh, you...

34
00:06:54.226 --> 00:06:55.584
families...

35
00:06:55.668 --> 00:06:57.018
...separated?

36
00:06:57.709 --> 00:06:58.876
I'm...

37
00:06:59.459 --> 00:07:00.784
going to...

38
00:07:01.834 --> 00:07:03.693
...Winchester Cathedral.

39
00:07:04.959 --> 00:07:06.676
You know where it is?

40
00:07:07.376 --> 00:07:09.084
Where?

41
00:07:20.084 --> 00:07:21.184
Mister.

42
00:07:21.584 --> 00:07:23.234
Did you say...

43
00:07:23.559 --> 00:07:26.043
Did you say "mister?"
Who said "mister?"

44
00:07:26.793 --> 00:07:31.009
- You speak English?
- We are from Winchester Cathedral.

45
00:07:32.184 --> 00:07:33.901
Say that again.

46
00:07:34.043 --> 00:07:36.943
We are from Winchester Cathedral.

47
00:07:39.418 --> 00:07:42.984
- You're kidding?
- We are students at the convent.

48
00:07:43.351 --> 00:07:45.051
You going there?

49
00:07:45.418 --> 00:07:47.693
Why do you want to go there?

50
00:07:48.876 --> 00:07:51.218
I'm helping to bury your father.

51
00:07:51.618 --> 00:07:53.518
Well, not your father father...

52
00:07:53.584 --> 00:07:55.851
- Father Ingleman.
- Father Ingleman, yeah.

53
00:07:55.901 --> 00:07:57.884
I'm helping burying him.

54
00:07:57.918 --> 00:08:00.618
Father Ingleman, I'm sending him off...

55
00:08:01.709 --> 00:08:03.826
...to heaven, wherever.

56
00:08:06.751 --> 00:08:08.493
You show me the way?

57
00:08:47.809 --> 00:08:51.293
Peng, move to the flank,
prepare to engage.

58
00:08:52.734 --> 00:08:55.243
- Damn it, are you deaf?
- Major Li,

59
00:08:55.334 --> 00:08:57.793
we are the last ones left.

60
00:08:57.918 --> 00:09:00.293
We should leave the city now.

61
00:09:01.709 --> 00:09:03.609
- Keep fighting.
- Yes sir.

62
00:09:22.168 --> 00:09:23.518
Got you!

63
00:10:16.334 --> 00:10:17.809
- Let's go.
- Yes sir.

64
00:10:26.551 --> 00:10:27.901
That way!

65
00:11:04.293 --> 00:11:06.276
Up there, on the right!

66
00:11:47.584 --> 00:11:49.459
On the left! Fire!

67
00:12:24.309 --> 00:12:25.793
Cover them!

68
00:12:46.876 --> 00:12:49.834
The Chinese army
didn't have adequate weapons

69
00:12:49.884 --> 00:12:53.351
so to destroy the enemy's tanks,
they employed a tactic from ancient warfare.

70
00:12:53.443 --> 00:12:58.276
They formed a human shield
to get a bomb close to the tanks.

71
00:12:58.293 --> 00:13:02.201
At the time, the Chinese people couldn't bear
the thought of losing their country,

72
00:13:02.293 --> 00:13:05.276
and such selfless acts were not uncommon.

73
00:16:23.001 --> 00:16:24.426
Zhen!

74
00:16:24.751 --> 00:16:26.493
Let me go!

75
00:16:29.168 --> 00:16:30.401
Zhen!

76
00:16:34.918 --> 00:16:36.359
Come on!

77
00:17:04.793 --> 00:17:06.234
Father Ingleman...

78
00:17:06.334 --> 00:17:08.543
...fly away.
- Fly away?

79
00:17:09.376 --> 00:17:12.226
On here, Japanese, bomb.

80
00:17:13.276 --> 00:17:15.726
- He flew away with the bomb, right.
- Yes.

81
00:17:15.793 --> 00:17:18.293
Why was the deceased out here?

82
00:17:18.668 --> 00:17:20.893
- Gu. All because of Gu.
- Gu?

83
00:17:20.959 --> 00:17:23.134
He said, bad smell.

84
00:17:23.501 --> 00:17:25.334
He moved the body here.

85
00:17:25.601 --> 00:17:28.534
- Who's Gu?
- Gu is our cook.

86
00:17:28.934 --> 00:17:31.801
He ran away.
He leaves some students here.

87
00:17:31.959 --> 00:17:34.676
Some students took away by parents.

88
00:17:34.859 --> 00:17:37.401
Some students, nowhere to go.

89
00:17:39.534 --> 00:17:42.418
So who's inside?
Just you and the girls?

90
00:17:43.001 --> 00:17:44.834
Just you and the girls.

91
00:17:47.376 --> 00:17:49.359
Even without a body...

92
00:17:49.476 --> 00:17:51.151
...you gotta pay me.

93
00:17:51.201 --> 00:17:54.134
- No.
- No, no, no... You gotta pay me.

94
00:17:54.243 --> 00:17:55.243
No.

95
00:17:55.293 --> 00:17:58.684
That's the rule.
There's nothing I can do about it.

96
00:17:58.709 --> 00:18:01.101
What I came through,
I should raise the price.

97
00:18:01.234 --> 00:18:03.618
- So is the money inside?
- No. No money.

98
00:18:03.643 --> 00:18:06.218
- Money? Inside?
- No.

99
00:18:06.459 --> 00:18:08.909
Come on.
There's no money inside?

100
00:18:08.918 --> 00:18:10.534
- No.
- Let's look.

101
00:18:10.543 --> 00:18:13.368
It's a Catholic church.
There's gotta be some cash inside.

102
00:18:13.418 --> 00:18:14.301
No.

103
00:18:14.393 --> 00:18:16.918
No? You say anything but no?

104
00:18:18.126 --> 00:18:20.443
Can you fix truck?

105
00:18:21.709 --> 00:18:24.101
Help us.
Leave Nanking.

106
00:18:24.501 --> 00:18:26.209
Fix this truck?

107
00:18:26.626 --> 00:18:28.151
For free?

108
00:18:28.809 --> 00:18:29.993
No.

109
00:18:30.668 --> 00:18:33.809
I can take parts, sell parts.
You got tools?

110
00:18:33.876 --> 00:18:35.001
No.

111
00:18:35.251 --> 00:18:37.018
Let's get inside.

112
00:18:40.043 --> 00:18:44.584
Zhen didn't even make a noise.
Even when they stabbed her over and over.

113
00:18:44.668 --> 00:18:46.876
Yet she didn't make a noise.

114
00:18:50.418 --> 00:18:52.393
It's all my fault.

115
00:18:53.376 --> 00:18:54.718
It's not.

116
00:18:54.918 --> 00:18:56.934
It is your fault.

117
00:18:57.668 --> 00:19:02.018
Your father promised to take us
on a boat and leave Nanking.

118
00:19:02.251 --> 00:19:04.943
Where is he?
He ran off.

119
00:19:05.084 --> 00:19:08.976
We waited and waited
and now the Japanese are here.

120
00:19:09.043 --> 00:19:13.593
Now the Japanese are everywhere,
and it's too late to go to the refuge.

121
00:19:15.584 --> 00:19:18.143
Zhen died because of your father!

122
00:19:19.151 --> 00:19:20.584
Shut up!

123
00:19:22.084 --> 00:19:24.093
What are you doing?

124
00:19:24.584 --> 00:19:26.001
Stop!

125
00:19:27.001 --> 00:19:28.959
- Stop fighting!
- Hey.

126
00:19:29.209 --> 00:19:30.434
Hey.

127
00:19:32.043 --> 00:19:33.743
Hey! Stop!

128
00:19:34.809 --> 00:19:36.076
Stop!

129
00:19:39.001 --> 00:19:41.709
I'm John. Hi.

130
00:19:42.501 --> 00:19:43.959
I'm American.

131
00:19:43.984 --> 00:19:46.526
He's the mortician for Father's funeral.

132
00:19:50.559 --> 00:19:53.984
I know it's hard.
But you've gotta stop fighting everybody.

133
00:19:54.251 --> 00:19:56.776
You know you two, you've seen enough...

134
00:19:56.851 --> 00:19:59.993
...seen enough tragedy for a lifetime today.

135
00:20:07.418 --> 00:20:10.109
I can't... um...
I'm not good with kids.

136
00:20:10.168 --> 00:20:11.601
Let's go.

137
00:20:11.709 --> 00:20:14.184
Oh, you want some flour?
You like some flour?

138
00:20:14.251 --> 00:20:17.334
- Make some bread for the girls.
- Buns.

139
00:20:18.001 --> 00:20:20.009
- Buns.
- Buns, whatever.

140
00:20:20.101 --> 00:20:21.668
Let's go find the collection box.

141
00:20:27.834 --> 00:20:28.959
Where?

142
00:20:29.043 --> 00:20:30.443
- Upstairs?
- No.

143
00:20:34.643 --> 00:20:36.101
Oh, nice.

144
00:20:36.543 --> 00:20:40.784
Forget going back to the refuge,
I think I'm bunking here, tonight.

145
00:20:45.793 --> 00:20:47.876
He's grim, who's that?

146
00:20:49.876 --> 00:20:52.218
- That Father Ingleman?
- Yes.

147
00:20:52.251 --> 00:20:56.584
These North Europeans they're all like,
you know, tuna, playwrights...

148
00:20:57.251 --> 00:20:58.684
...not much fun.

149
00:20:58.709 --> 00:21:02.918
Oh, look at that face,
he's ruining the...

150
00:21:03.709 --> 00:21:05.793
What do you call it? Feng... Fengshui?

151
00:21:05.959 --> 00:21:09.676
Well, I can't have a priest...
I can't have a priest staring at me...

152
00:21:09.684 --> 00:21:12.009
...while I'm sleeping.
- No. No, no, no...

153
00:21:13.101 --> 00:21:14.576
My father.

154
00:21:16.726 --> 00:21:18.009
Me...

155
00:21:18.576 --> 00:21:19.876
orphan...

156
00:21:20.018 --> 00:21:23.093
...adopted.
- I'm sorry. But I just...

157
00:21:23.109 --> 00:21:26.159
Ah, it's not good for me
to have a priest

158
00:21:26.226 --> 00:21:28.118
staring at me while I'm sleeping.

159
00:21:28.351 --> 00:21:29.601
I can't.

160
00:21:29.626 --> 00:21:32.793
Please, I gotta just... there, better.

161
00:21:33.209 --> 00:21:34.793
You got any drink around here?

162
00:21:34.959 --> 00:21:37.943
- No.
- You're a church. You got wine, something?

163
00:21:38.084 --> 00:21:40.268
- Nothing.
- Nothing?

164
00:21:48.809 --> 00:21:51.084
- No.
- No, no, no...

165
00:21:51.959 --> 00:21:53.951
That's a shaving kit.

166
00:21:54.626 --> 00:21:56.284
What a jerk!

167
00:21:57.043 --> 00:21:59.209
I said you'e a jerk!

168
00:21:59.893 --> 00:22:01.718
What did you say your name was?

169
00:22:01.751 --> 00:22:03.984
- George Chen.
- George.

170
00:22:04.518 --> 00:22:05.951
Tomorrow...

171
00:22:06.418 --> 00:22:08.284
you fix truck...

172
00:22:08.934 --> 00:22:10.359
...help us.

173
00:22:11.751 --> 00:22:13.201
Fix truck?

174
00:22:14.584 --> 00:22:16.076
No money!

175
00:22:17.043 --> 00:22:18.701
Money, George.

176
00:22:24.209 --> 00:22:26.793
Gu. Open the door, it's Ling.

177
00:22:27.226 --> 00:22:29.143
Can you hear me?

178
00:22:29.626 --> 00:22:30.759
Gu!

179
00:22:30.826 --> 00:22:32.401
Open up.

180
00:22:32.834 --> 00:22:34.401
It's Ling.

181
00:22:34.418 --> 00:22:36.501
- Did you really make a deal with him?
- Of course.

182
00:22:36.543 --> 00:22:38.501
Otherwise I wouldn't have brought you here.

183
00:22:38.559 --> 00:22:40.626
Gu. Gu.

184
00:22:40.793 --> 00:22:44.884
Open the door, it's Ling.
Gu, have you gone deaf?

185
00:22:45.001 --> 00:22:46.434
Someone's here.

186
00:22:46.501 --> 00:22:49.293
- Where's Gu? Ask him to come out.
- Go to the refuge on the west side.

187
00:22:49.393 --> 00:22:53.426
- Leave now, go to the refuge.
- No, we're here for Gu.

188
00:22:53.459 --> 00:22:55.993
- Gu's not here.
- Bullshit! Get out of my way!

189
00:22:56.101 --> 00:22:58.668
Gu told me,
this church is under Western protection.

190
00:22:58.726 --> 00:23:00.059
The Japanese can't come in.

191
00:23:00.126 --> 00:23:03.634
Bastard! I served Gu all night for free,
he promised to let us stay.

192
00:23:03.668 --> 00:23:05.709
- Ask that bastard Gu to come out!
- He's really not here.

193
00:23:05.793 --> 00:23:07.693
- How come?
- He ran off this morning.

194
00:23:07.834 --> 00:23:10.034
You should go to the refuge.

195
00:23:29.876 --> 00:23:31.593
We're not leaving.

196
00:23:45.459 --> 00:23:47.376
Hey! How dare you!

197
00:23:48.501 --> 00:23:50.809
- Hurry.
- Go to the refuge!

198
00:23:50.918 --> 00:23:51.851
To the refuge!

199
00:23:51.918 --> 00:23:54.243
The refuge doesn't even
have space left for maggots.

200
00:23:54.309 --> 00:23:57.076
Please, have some mercy and let us in.

201
00:23:59.401 --> 00:24:01.034
Don't jump!

202
00:24:26.126 --> 00:24:29.143
- They're from the red-light district.
- What's that?

203
00:24:29.168 --> 00:24:30.718
It means brothel.

204
00:24:37.001 --> 00:24:39.651
They were the famous women
of the Qin Huai River.

205
00:24:39.684 --> 00:24:44.159
The myths surrounding them
were as ancient as the city of Nanking.

206
00:24:51.459 --> 00:24:54.518
- That's a Westerner!
- Is he a priest?

207
00:24:54.584 --> 00:24:55.809
No way.

208
00:24:55.876 --> 00:25:00.218
- What kind of priest would be such a flirt?
- Who cares, as long as he can protect us.

209
00:25:00.276 --> 00:25:01.551
True.

210
00:25:36.184 --> 00:25:37.968
Come up here, huh?

211
00:25:38.084 --> 00:25:42.343
This was stolen from the bowels of hell.

212
00:25:42.559 --> 00:25:44.784
Long time not make bread.

213
00:25:44.851 --> 00:25:47.401
Long time not make bread? No bread?

214
00:25:47.418 --> 00:25:49.934
Not tonight, tonight we're having bread.

215
00:25:52.709 --> 00:25:55.493
These women quickly took over the cellar.

216
00:25:55.668 --> 00:25:58.193
It was once a filthy, messy place,

217
00:25:58.209 --> 00:25:59.909
but within hours,

218
00:26:00.001 --> 00:26:02.293
they had transformed it
into the Qin Huai River.

219
00:26:02.309 --> 00:26:05.976
The fragrance of rouge and perfume
danced up through the air.

220
00:26:27.251 --> 00:26:29.851
I can smell the bread.
We are coming up!

221
00:26:42.151 --> 00:26:44.076
I couldn't stop them.

222
00:26:47.834 --> 00:26:49.043
Hello.

223
00:26:52.334 --> 00:26:56.501
I remember,
when I first saw these women,

224
00:26:56.543 --> 00:26:59.484
they were tramps,
parading around in their lingerie,

225
00:26:59.559 --> 00:27:03.009
not the graceful ladies the legends
of Qin Huai had portrayed them to be.

226
00:27:06.918 --> 00:27:08.951
Look, this should be good.

227
00:27:26.459 --> 00:27:28.793
George, you little shit,

228
00:27:28.818 --> 00:27:31.051
you said there was no wine here.

229
00:27:31.334 --> 00:27:34.284
- Excuse me.
- What's he saying?

230
00:27:36.668 --> 00:27:38.509
Holy hooch!

231
00:27:40.059 --> 00:27:42.559
How dare you drink the wine!
Now the Westerner knows about the wine.

232
00:27:42.601 --> 00:27:44.226
We sell the wine to raise
money for orphans.

233
00:27:44.293 --> 00:27:47.093
We're all orphans.
We also need help.

234
00:27:47.193 --> 00:27:48.834
That's right.

235
00:27:49.326 --> 00:27:51.526
- What are they saying?
- They said they're orphans!

236
00:27:51.709 --> 00:27:52.718
Orphans?

237
00:27:52.793 --> 00:27:55.293
Well, I'd like to adopt all of you, right now.

238
00:27:55.418 --> 00:27:59.334
Adopt all of us?
You would not be able to cope.

239
00:28:02.084 --> 00:28:04.376
You are not the only one
who speak English!

240
00:28:04.443 --> 00:28:05.868
That's right!

241
00:28:07.209 --> 00:28:08.918
You speak English?

242
00:28:21.834 --> 00:28:23.884
The Westerner is a playboy.

243
00:28:23.976 --> 00:28:28.718
Of course! Haven't you heard?
Westerners with beards are the horniest!

244
00:28:29.234 --> 00:28:31.493
No wonder she is
the top girl of the Qin Huai River.

245
00:28:31.559 --> 00:28:34.776
Mo, use all of your skills.
Seduce him!

246
00:28:34.918 --> 00:28:36.251
That's right.

247
00:28:36.318 --> 00:28:39.334
Make the big nose go crazy for us!

248
00:28:47.351 --> 00:28:49.176
My name is John.

249
00:28:50.501 --> 00:28:52.876
- And you are?
- Yu Mo.

250
00:28:52.934 --> 00:28:54.351
Yu Mo.

251
00:28:54.559 --> 00:28:56.051
I like that.

252
00:28:56.251 --> 00:29:00.268
So what do you and your companions do?

253
00:29:00.893 --> 00:29:04.343
- We are kindergarten teachers.
- Really? Kindergarten teachers.

254
00:29:04.376 --> 00:29:05.243
Shameless.

255
00:29:05.309 --> 00:29:07.234
And you?
What do you do?

256
00:29:07.334 --> 00:29:09.251
I'm also a kindergarten teacher.

257
00:29:11.876 --> 00:29:13.276
So as,

258
00:29:13.376 --> 00:29:15.051
teacher to teacher,

259
00:29:15.101 --> 00:29:16.451
you wanna...

260
00:29:16.709 --> 00:29:19.701
...get together and have a cup of joe.

261
00:29:19.801 --> 00:29:21.734
What're those two yapping about? Tell me.

262
00:29:21.809 --> 00:29:24.659
Nothing. He's asking your price.

263
00:29:24.918 --> 00:29:28.218
I told him.
He thinks you are too cheap.

264
00:30:09.751 --> 00:30:12.568
