has a way of just...

528
01:04:28.259 --> 01:04:29.634
...you know.

529
01:04:31.518 --> 01:04:34.201
What do you think
the Japanese are up to?

530
01:04:34.226 --> 01:04:36.918
Are they really here
to protect the students?

531
01:04:42.834 --> 01:04:45.784
We were counting on having you
help us leave Nanking.

532
01:04:45.809 --> 01:04:49.434
But I guess now you'll have to
stay here and be a priest.

533
01:04:51.143 --> 01:04:52.893
Yeah, right.

534
01:04:54.893 --> 01:04:56.159
Priest.

535
01:04:59.126 --> 01:05:01.943
Actually, I came to tell you,
our offer is still good.

536
01:05:02.334 --> 01:05:04.551
We still want you to help us escape.

537
01:05:04.559 --> 01:05:07.068
As soon as the Japanese guards are gone.

538
01:05:08.168 --> 01:05:10.684
Just now the ladies were having a bet.

539
01:05:10.709 --> 01:05:14.468
They said that hero or no hero,
you don't stand a chance

540
01:05:14.543 --> 01:05:16.918
when you're up against a beauty like me.

541
01:05:17.501 --> 01:05:19.326
Don't flatter yourself.

542
01:05:20.584 --> 01:05:22.034
We'll see.

543
01:05:50.918 --> 01:05:52.776
Did you like it?

544
01:05:55.209 --> 01:05:59.109
I only have one string.
It sound like a beggar's plea.

545
01:06:08.168 --> 01:06:11.109
You're Pu Sheng.
Born in the Pu region?

546
01:06:11.584 --> 01:06:13.734
My family is also from there.

547
01:06:13.984 --> 01:06:16.718
When you're healthy,
I'll take you to the biggest dance hall,

548
01:06:16.793 --> 01:06:18.826
to see the prettiest girls.

549
01:06:19.793 --> 01:06:21.143
Thank you.

550
01:06:22.009 --> 01:06:25.559
Little hometown fellow,
don't thank me, marry me.

551
01:06:28.926 --> 01:06:31.468
I'll work in the fields with you.

552
01:06:32.668 --> 01:06:35.368
I don't have... fields.

553
01:06:36.109 --> 01:06:38.168
What do you have then?

554
01:06:38.751 --> 01:06:41.084
I don't have anything.

555
01:06:41.543 --> 01:06:44.318
Then I'll play my pipa everyday.

556
01:06:44.376 --> 01:06:48.626
When I play, you hold out a bowl.
We'll beg for food and feed your mom.

557
01:06:49.293 --> 01:06:51.359
I don't have a mother.

558
01:06:51.459 --> 01:06:54.059
Everyone in my family is dead.

559
01:07:57.168 --> 01:07:59.501
If you had just come with me...

560
01:07:59.584 --> 01:08:01.509
...this wouldn't have happened.

561
01:08:01.543 --> 01:08:05.159
You were so stubborn,
and wouldn't leave without your classmates.

562
01:08:05.268 --> 01:08:08.268
How could I have gotten
that many boat tickets?

563
01:08:08.543 --> 01:08:12.051
Because of you,
I'm staying in Nanking.

564
01:08:17.251 --> 01:08:19.618
Tell me, what's this?

565
01:08:20.001 --> 01:08:21.609
Explain to me,

566
01:08:21.659 --> 01:08:23.943
why do you do this?

567
01:08:26.918 --> 01:08:29.943
If I don't do this,
I can't survive.

568
01:08:30.168 --> 01:08:32.076
I'm doing this for you.

569
01:08:32.168 --> 01:08:35.518
You must believe me,
I would never do anything bad.

570
01:08:35.559 --> 01:08:36.826
Daughter,

571
01:08:37.043 --> 01:08:40.134
I will find a way
to get you out of Nanking.

572
01:08:51.293 --> 01:08:54.068
No wonder there were no
boat tickets. Traitor!

573
01:09:27.793 --> 01:09:29.226
You work for the Japanese?

574
01:09:29.293 --> 01:09:32.093
Since I cannot save my country,
cannot save others,

575
01:09:32.168 --> 01:09:34.193
I can only try to save myself.

576
01:09:34.293 --> 01:09:36.459
I'm already doing my best, you know.

577
01:09:36.568 --> 01:09:39.234
Do you think it's easy
working for the Japanese?

578
01:09:39.293 --> 01:09:41.401
It's good you work for the Japanese,
that helps us.

579
01:09:41.484 --> 01:09:43.309
What is your plan for your daughter?

580
01:09:43.793 --> 01:09:46.976
I would like to try,
and use my connections with the Japanese

581
01:09:47.043 --> 01:09:49.259
to get my daughter  out of the city.

582
01:09:50.293 --> 01:09:52.493
- Not to the refuge?
- The refuge?

583
01:09:52.518 --> 01:09:54.826
It's not safe there at all!

584
01:09:57.043 --> 01:09:59.559
What's your plan for the rest of the girls?

585
01:10:03.684 --> 01:10:05.193
Mr Meng?

586
01:10:06.101 --> 01:10:09.626
I have this truck.
If I can get the right tools,

587
01:10:09.859 --> 01:10:11.909
then maybe I can get it started.

588
01:10:11.976 --> 01:10:13.818
Can you help me?

589
01:10:15.543 --> 01:10:17.168
I have a list here.

590
01:10:17.209 --> 01:10:20.018
Mr Meng.
I need these tools.

591
01:10:20.168 --> 01:10:22.068
Can you help me get them?

592
01:10:22.326 --> 01:10:24.676
You're the only one who
can get them for me.

593
01:10:25.084 --> 01:10:27.209
I need these tools.

594
01:10:30.501 --> 01:10:33.034
I need these tools.
Take this.

595
01:10:33.684 --> 01:10:35.076
Take this.

596
01:10:39.759 --> 01:10:41.701
If I fix the truck...

597
01:10:42.368 --> 01:10:45.968
- If I fix the truck, what then?
- How would I know?

598
01:10:48.043 --> 01:10:51.768
Wait, wait. If I fix the truck,
what would I need then?

599
01:10:52.043 --> 01:10:55.359
- Of course you'll need a permit.
- I need a permit?

600
01:10:56.709 --> 01:10:58.584
I need a permit.

601
01:10:58.918 --> 01:11:00.676
Don't look at me.

602
01:11:00.751 --> 01:11:02.459
It's too risky!

603
01:11:25.876 --> 01:11:27.876
Even if you fix the truck,

604
01:11:27.918 --> 01:11:30.159
how would you get past
the Japanese guards?

605
01:11:30.834 --> 01:11:32.468
I don't know.

606
01:11:34.626 --> 01:11:36.684
I don't know how long...

607
01:11:36.851 --> 01:11:38.951
...the guards will stay here.

608
01:11:39.543 --> 01:11:43.401
But I want to get that truck started
for when they leave.

609
01:11:43.484 --> 01:11:47.043
It seems that you know
more than just drinking.

610
01:11:56.126 --> 01:11:59.359
I don't think she likes seeing us together.
She has a crush on you.

611
01:11:59.501 --> 01:12:00.626
Really?

612
01:12:03.959 --> 01:12:06.076
You know, I was like her.

613
01:12:07.168 --> 01:12:08.351
Yeah?

614
01:12:10.001 --> 01:12:12.893
I was at a convent for six years.

615
01:12:17.084 --> 01:12:19.751
That's where you learned your English?

616
01:12:26.126 --> 01:12:27.576
What happened?

617
01:12:28.459 --> 01:12:31.126
Just another story of misfortune.

618
01:12:31.293 --> 01:12:34.501
It wouldn't interest
a passerby like yourself.

619
01:12:34.876 --> 01:12:36.426
Yeah, it would.

620
01:12:36.626 --> 01:12:38.009
Tell me.

621
01:12:41.668 --> 01:12:43.076
Tell me.

622
01:12:46.334 --> 01:12:49.193
I was never meant to be like this.

623
01:12:52.543 --> 01:12:53.959
Never mind.

624
01:12:55.584 --> 01:12:57.134
You know what?

625
01:12:57.168 --> 01:13:00.268
I was the best in my English class,

626
01:13:00.334 --> 01:13:02.609
but everyone used to mock me.

627
01:13:02.668 --> 01:13:05.293
They said I put on airs and graces

628
01:13:05.334 --> 01:13:09.043
and acted like
I was the Queen of England.

629
01:13:11.668 --> 01:13:14.718
Well, that's not
what you were going to tell me, but...

630
01:13:15.084 --> 01:13:16.968
So... the Queen of England.

631
01:13:17.084 --> 01:13:18.668
You mean you're not?

632
01:13:18.751 --> 01:13:20.476
I thought... yeah.

633
01:13:22.584 --> 01:13:25.851
Like Shu, I too had a crush on someone.

634
01:13:25.959 --> 01:13:29.334
But he was a young, fresh-faced guy...

635
01:13:30.334 --> 01:13:32.743
got the most beautiful eyes...

636
01:13:34.668 --> 01:13:37.068
...not a dirty, bearded man like you.

637
01:13:41.793 --> 01:13:43.009
Okay.

638
01:14:37.459 --> 01:14:38.893
It's rotten.

639
01:14:41.334 --> 01:14:42.576
Sister.

640
01:14:45.651 --> 01:14:47.443
What are you saying?

641
01:14:47.501 --> 01:14:48.684
Sister...

642
01:14:48.876 --> 01:14:50.084
Hurry...

643
01:14:51.359 --> 01:14:53.651
Pu Sheng, I'm here.

644
01:14:55.126 --> 01:14:56.368
Thunder...

645
01:14:57.209 --> 01:14:59.393
What are you trying to say?

646
01:15:00.168 --> 01:15:02.251
Rain... Rain...

647
01:15:05.776 --> 01:15:07.318
What rain?

648
01:15:07.793 --> 01:15:10.326
It's death weeping for you.

649
01:15:11.068 --> 01:15:15.334
The wheat is drying outside...

650
01:15:16.943 --> 01:15:20.293
Don't let it get soaked.

651
01:16:16.334 --> 01:16:20.126
That was the soldier that the officer brought.
I heard he was about our age.

652
01:16:20.584 --> 01:16:21.909
Which officer?

653
01:16:22.001 --> 01:16:24.668
The officer who saved us that day.

654
01:16:25.401 --> 01:16:27.901
He hid the soldier inside the cellar,

655
01:16:28.001 --> 01:16:30.343
and the women were taking care of him.

656
01:16:30.418 --> 01:16:33.434
Actually those women from the brothel...

657
01:16:33.501 --> 01:16:35.284
...are not that bad.

658
01:16:36.293 --> 01:16:37.709
Where's Dou?

659
01:16:40.134 --> 01:16:41.843
Lan's missing too.

660
01:16:41.876 --> 01:16:43.068
Really?

661
01:16:43.318 --> 01:16:47.426
- Haven't seen them for a while.
- Are they still in the cellar?

662
01:16:47.443 --> 01:16:49.293
Have you seen Dou?

663
01:16:55.793 --> 01:16:58.209
Dou and Lan got out.

664
01:16:58.634 --> 01:17:00.643
How?
Where did they go?

665
01:17:00.818 --> 01:17:03.634
Dou insisted on getting pipa strings.

666
01:17:03.693 --> 01:17:06.068
She wanted to play the pipa for Pu Sheng.

667
01:17:06.126 --> 01:17:09.276
She said he had a hard life,
and he was like her brother.

668
01:17:09.318 --> 01:17:12.034
She wanted to play something nice for him,

669
01:17:12.126 --> 01:17:15.543
but one string wasn't enough,
she needed three more.

670
01:17:15.709 --> 01:17:17.618
What about Lan?
Why did she go?

671
01:17:17.718 --> 01:17:20.626
She said she left her earrings behind.

672
01:17:21.251 --> 01:17:23.951
How could they leave?
The Japanese are guarding the gates.

673
01:17:24.051 --> 01:17:26.701
I don't know how they got out.

674
01:17:26.751 --> 01:17:30.609
They disappeared when it was dark.
Dou said that...

675
01:17:30.668 --> 01:17:33.118
...if she didn't go soon
it would be too late for him.

676
01:17:33.193 --> 01:17:37.426
- Why didn't you stop them!
- I tried, but it didn't work!

677
01:17:43.251 --> 01:17:46.543
- What happened?
- Dou and Lan snuck out on their own.

678
01:17:47.293 --> 01:17:49.018
Dou and Lan?

679
01:17:49.809 --> 01:17:52.626
- How? How did they leave?
- I don't know.

680
01:17:52.709 --> 01:17:54.759
- You know when?
- No.

681
01:17:55.234 --> 01:17:56.226
Where did they go?

682
01:17:56.318 --> 01:17:59.184
They went back to our brothel
to get pipa strings.

683
01:18:10.026 --> 01:18:12.126
And you want me to...
go find them?

684
01:18:12.193 --> 01:18:13.293
Yeah.

685
01:18:14.859 --> 01:18:17.426
- Mo, I'm not sure...
- Please.

686
01:18:19.318 --> 01:18:21.209
Please. Please!

687
01:18:30.376 --> 01:18:33.634
Alright, it's safer for me
than anyone else, so I'll try.

688
01:18:33.834 --> 01:18:35.159
I'll try.

689
01:18:35.168 --> 01:18:38.268
If I can leave.
If they let me leave.

690
01:18:39.526 --> 01:18:41.418
Candles, food.

691
01:18:41.776 --> 01:18:43.626
There is no food.

692
01:18:43.734 --> 01:18:45.209
They need food.

693
01:18:45.234 --> 01:18:48.051
With no food.
No singing.

694
01:18:48.293 --> 01:18:51.168
Hasegawa asks girls to sing.

695
01:18:52.559 --> 01:18:54.651
Singing, for the girls.

696
01:18:54.668 --> 01:18:56.818
Hasegawa asks.

697
01:18:58.151 --> 01:19:01.126
But no singing with no food.

698
01:19:01.609 --> 01:19:03.609
And candles for Hasegawa.

699
01:19:03.651 --> 01:19:04.584
I go get food.

700
01:19:04.751 --> 01:19:07.734
Girl sing. Hasegawa happy. Yes?
I go now.

701
01:19:07.918 --> 01:19:10.276
George, you're not coming.

702
01:19:10.834 --> 01:19:12.901
I go, for food?

703
01:19:12.934 --> 01:19:14.918
Yes?
George, you're not coming.

704
01:19:15.351 --> 01:19:16.984
Go back inside!
Yes?

705
01:19:17.334 --> 01:19:19.201
Make Hasegawa happy.

706
01:19:19.501 --> 01:19:21.843
- Go!
- This is fine, I go. Thank you.

707
01:19:25.693 --> 01:19:27.709
Officer, is he allowed to leave?

708
01:19:27.876 --> 01:19:31.343
We've been told not to let the girls leave.
But he's the priest.

709
01:19:59.251 --> 01:20:00.359
Terry?

710
01:20:02.918 --> 01:20:03.943
Terry.

711
01:20:03.959 --> 01:20:05.109
John?

712
01:20:06.084 --> 01:20:07.976
I tried getting back,
I tried getting back to the refuge.

713
01:20:08.126 --> 01:20:09.151
I got stuck.

714
01:20:09.251 --> 01:20:11.568
I couldn't get back.
I was trying to get back. I'm sorry.

715
01:20:11.651 --> 01:20:13.918
I thought you were...
I figured you were dead.

716
01:20:14.084 --> 01:20:16.359
I'm looking for two women,
they got shiny dresses.

717
01:20:16.393 --> 01:20:18.251
I need to find them.
They are in trouble.

718
01:20:18.318 --> 01:20:19.918
Why are you dressed like this?
What is this?

719
01:20:20.084 --> 01:20:23.518
I got drunk, I woke up,
I was just, dressed as a priest.

720
01:20:25.384 --> 01:20:26.334
Who is this?

721
01:20:26.484 --> 01:20:28.751
This is George. This is George.
Have you seen them?

722
01:20:28.834 --> 01:20:30.234
- Seen who?
- The women!

723
01:20:30.284 --> 01:20:32.584
There're women piled up
all over the street.

724
01:20:32.751 --> 01:20:35.551
- You haven't seen them?
- No, I haven't seen any women. No.

725
01:20:35.626 --> 01:20:37.501
You think it's safe to be
looking for women right now?

726
01:20:37.668 --> 01:20:39.793
- Can you help me with tools?
- Tools for what?

727
01:20:39.818 --> 01:20:42.118
- I gotta fix a truck.
- Fix a truck for what?

728
01:20:42.168 --> 01:20:44.201
I gotta help George,
I gotta help some girls,

729
01:20:44.293 --> 01:20:46.209
I gotta help some women,
they're prostitutes,

730
01:20:46.276 --> 01:20:47.959
- and I gotta help them.
- What? Are you kidding me?

731
01:20:48.026 --> 01:20:50.584
You're talking about prostitutes
and trucks, and tools.

732
01:20:50.626 --> 01:20:53.776
I'm talking about not dying in China.
I'm leaving right now.

733
01:20:54.126 --> 01:20:56.793
- You're leaving Nanking right now?
- Do you wanna go?

734
01:20:57.001 --> 01:20:59.159
There's a boat. It's waiting for us.

735
01:20:59.334 --> 01:21:02.768
I'm leaving right now!
If you wanna go, then let's go!

736
01:21:03.484 --> 01:21:05.368
It's your last chance.

737
01:21:09.859 --> 01:21:11.568
I gotta find them.
I can't leave.

738
01:21:12.001 --> 01:21:15.168
- Are you kidding me right now?
- I'll see you, Terry!

739
01:21:15.626 --> 01:21:17.201
I'll see ya.

740
01:22:18.009 --> 01:22:19.859
Take off your coat!

741
01:22:20.418 --> 01:22:21.518
Hurry!

742
01:22:24.176 --> 01:22:26.343
They went that way.

743
01:22:28.751 --> 01:22:30.543
Those are their coats.

744
01:22:31.918 --> 01:22:36.751
- Look! Those are young girls' coats!
- The girls can't be far.

745
01:22:45.918 --> 01:22:48.351
Oh no, I dropped the strings!

746
01:22:49.034 --> 01:22:51.834
- Forget it.
- No, I have to find them.

747
01:23:42.126 --> 01:23:44.459
- Over there!
- Don't shoot!

748
01:23:46.168 --> 01:23:46.959
Lan!

749
01:23:47.401 --> 01:23:48.393
Lan!

750
01:23:48.626 --> 01:23:50.126
Don't run!

751
01:23:57.584 --> 01:24:00.034
Bitch! Go to hell!

752
01:24:00.193 --> 01:24:02.526
We'll deal with her later.
Let's catch the other one.

753
01:24:02.584 --> 01:24:03.793
Let's go!

754
01:24:14.834 --> 01:24:16.501
Here she is!

755
01:24:33.626 --> 01:24:35.701
Why am I always the last one?

756
01:24:35.709 --> 01:24:38.143
- You shouldn't have shot the other girl.
- It's not fair!

757
01:24:38.168 --> 01:24:39.168
Hurry!

758
01:24:47.709 --> 01:24:49.126
Fuck you!

759
01:24:49.176 --> 01:24:50.959
Fuck you all!

760
01:24:56.801 --> 01:24:59.376
Bitch! You bit me!

761
01:24:59.859 --> 01:25:01.909
I'll kill you!

762
01:25:07.084 --> 01:25:10.393
What an idiot! You got bitten!
You can only handle the dead one upstairs!

763
01:26:13.651 --> 01:26:15.684
Is it? George, yes?

764
01:26:16.418 --> 01:26:17.659
Is it?

765
01:26:19.793 --> 01:26:21.793
Is it? Yes?

766
01:26:33.251 --> 01:26:35.543
Stay there, stay there.

767
01:27:07.334 --> 01:27:09.176
They were on their way back.

768
01:27:14.701 --> 01:27:17.168
It was a stray bullet or... maybe...

769
01:27:17.334 --> 01:27:18.884
I don't know.

770
01:27:22.793 --> 01:27:24.676
I don't think they suffered.

771
01:27:25.251 --> 01:27:26.893
I don't think so.

772
01:27:28.751 --> 01:27:30.509
Is that true?

773
01:27:31.584 --> 01:27:32.668
Yes.

774
01:27:37.043 --> 01:27:38.343
He said...

775
01:27:38.609 --> 01:27:41.784
Dou and Lan were hit by stray bullets...

776
01:27:42.451 --> 01:27:44.543
...that they didn't suffer.

777
01:27:57.934 --> 01:27:59.284
Come in.

778
01:28:00.251 --> 01:28:01.459
George.

779
01:28:02.001 --> 01:28:03.751
Come in. George.

780
01:28:04.668 --> 01:28:06.034
It's me.

781
01:28:09.001 --> 01:28:11.018
I only have two minutes.

782
01:28:11.709 --> 01:28:13.959
The guards finally let me in.

783
01:28:14.418 --> 01:28:16.526
These tools, you need.

784
01:28:19.418 --> 01:28:20.701
Thank you.

785
01:28:21.376 --> 01:28:24.709
Now, listen to me.
This permit was for my daughter.

786
01:28:24.726 --> 01:28:25.701
Right.

787
01:28:25.809 --> 01:28:27.793
But I can't carry out my plan.

788
01:28:28.751 --> 01:28:30.684
You are my only hope now.

789
01:28:31.734 --> 01:28:33.501
The Japanese don't trust me any more.

790
01:28:33.568 --> 01:28:35.718
You are a Westerner.
You can help her.

791
01:28:37.126 --> 01:28:39.584
My daughter wouldn't leave
without her classmates.

792
01:28:39.959 --> 01:28:42.643
Please think of a way to
get her out of Nanking.

793
01:28:42.709 --> 01:28:45.718
This permit is only good for a short time.

794
01:28:45.943 --> 01:28:47.909
When you manage to leave the church,

795
01:28:47.918 --> 01:28:50.201
remember, head west.

796
01:28:50.501 --> 01:28:52.934
There's a way out of the city there.

797
01:28:53.293 --> 01:28:54.834
I have to go.

798
01:28:54.851 --> 01:28:57.001
Thank you, Mr Meng.
Mr Meng, thank you.

799
01:28:57.068 --> 01:28:58.626
Mr Meng, with your connections

800
01:28:58.793 --> 01:29:00.434
is there anything else
you can do for us?

801
01:29:00.501 --> 01:29:02.643
No, no, sorry. John...

802
01:29:03.084 --> 01:29:05.326
...I'm handing my daughter over to you.

803
01:29:06.876 --> 01:29:09.018
I have promised her mother,

804
01:29:09.026 --> 01:29:11.034
I will take good care of her.

805
01:29:11.084 --> 01:29:12.026
Okay.

806
01:29:12.168 --> 01:29:13.393
Please.

807
01:29:15.426 --> 01:29:17.759
Okay, Mr Meng, thank you.

808
01:29:17.918 --> 01:29:20.959
Thank you for this.
You are a good man.

809
01:29:21.918 --> 01:29:23.893
In the eyes of my daughter...

810
01:29:23.984 --> 01:29:25.684
I'm a bad man...

811
01:29:25.751 --> 01:29:27.659
...a traitor.
- No.

812
01:29:28.793 --> 01:29:30.159
Thank you.

813
01:30:33.401 --> 01:30:36.451
Damn Mosquito, her cat ran off.
She went up to look for it.

814
01:31:05.584 --> 01:31:06.809
Good.

815
01:31:07.318 --> 01:31:09.134
You sing very well.

816
01:31:23.776 --> 01:31:26.368
Haven't I told you?
You can't come out!

817
01:31:27.543 --> 01:31:28.776
Officer...

818
01:31:29.068 --> 01:31:32.001
...this student has lost her uniform.

819
01:31:32.443 --> 01:31:35.651
Because we wanted
to look our best today,

820
01:31:36.109 --> 01:31:40.084
we asked her not to
participate in the performance.

821
01:31:40.709 --> 01:31:42.743
Please forgive the intrusion.

822
01:31:55.318 --> 01:31:56.501
Father...

823
01:31:56.959 --> 01:31:59.318
...I would like to announce
some good news.

824
01:31:59.609 --> 01:32:03.876
Tomorrow our division is celebrating
the successful occupation of Nanking.

825
01:32:04.209 --> 01:32:07.451
Esteemed Father,
on behalf of all the officers,

826
01:32:07.526 --> 01:32:11.826
I would like to invite your church choir
to perform and celebrate with us.

827
01:32:22.209 --> 01:32:24.651
This is the official invitation.

828
01:32:29.109 --> 01:32:31.693
They are asking us to
sing at a party tomorrow.

829
01:32:35.276 --> 01:32:38.451
This is a very kind invitation,
Mr Hasegawa.

830
01:32:39.084 --> 01:32:42.459
However, unfortunately,
the children will not be able to attend.

831
01:32:42.959 --> 01:32:45.451
- Why not?
- Sir, they're very young.

832
01:32:45.793 --> 01:32:49.851
I'm not sure that it is appropriate
for them to attend an adults' party.

833
01:32:49.918 --> 01:32:53.359
As their guardian and protector,
that's my responsibility.

834
01:32:53.751 --> 01:32:55.659
We thank you very much.

835
01:32:57.209 --> 01:33:00.226
I am sorry.
This is an order from above.

836
01:33:00.293 --> 01:33:02.101
I cannot disobey.

837
01:33:06.984 --> 01:33:09.568
Sir, please think about the girls.

838
01:33:09.818 --> 01:33:12.084
I can see that you are a man with culture.

839
01:33:12.151 --> 01:33:15.901
Last time you played us a beautiful song,
for people far from home.

840
01:33:16.293 --> 01:33:19.409
You missed the rivers and hills.

841
01:33:19.776 --> 01:33:22.518
Please consider that theirs
have been destroyed,

842
01:33:22.593 --> 01:33:25.076
they have no home, nothing.

843
01:33:25.668 --> 01:33:27.176
They are living in hell.

844
01:33:27.409 --> 01:33:30.801
With this invitation,
you are asking them to celebrate that.

845
01:33:31.334 --> 01:33:34.268
I know that you understand.
With respect, sir,

846
01:33:34.526 --> 01:33:37.368
I cannot allow that.
I think that is...

847
01:33:38.984 --> 01:33:41.101
I think that is brutal, sir.

848
01:33:43.751 --> 01:33:45.459
Please remember...

849
01:33:45.901 --> 01:33:49.693
...tomorrow at four in the afternoon,
a car will come to pick up the students.

850
01:33:49.709 --> 01:33:52.001
I am carrying out military orders.

851
01:33:52.068 --> 01:33:53.684
Mr Hasegawa...

852
01:33:54.626 --> 01:33:57.584
...you tell me what will happen
at these celebrations.

853
01:34:01.918 --> 01:34:04.209
Mr Hasegawa. Mr Hasegawa.

854
01:34:07.126 --> 01:34:09.909
You said you posted
guards for our security.

855
01:34:09.943 --> 01:34:13.543
Have you been keeping these girls
locked up until these celebrations?

856
01:34:17.693 --> 01:34:20.043
The children cannot go.

857
01:34:22.126 --> 01:34:23.426
Mr Hasegawa.

858
01:34:24.268 --> 01:34:25.651
Mr Hasegawa.

859
01:34:25.926 --> 01:34:28.018
The children cannot go!

860
01:34:29.526 --> 01:34:31.284
The children cannot go!

861
01:34:46.584 --> 01:34:49.001
One, two, three, four,

862
01:34:49.068 --> 01:34:51.518
five, six, seven, eight,

863
01:34:51.584 --> 01:34:53.351
nine, ten, eleven,

864
01:34:53.418 --> 01:34:55.468
twelve, thirteen.

865
01:34:56.751 --> 01:34:57.984
All...

866
01:34:59.001 --> 01:35:00.318
...must go!

867
01:35:22.293 --> 01:35:23.726
Father John?

868
01:35:25.251 --> 01:35:29.826
What do the Japanese want us to do?
Do they want us to sing?

869
01:35:30.126 --> 01:35:31.334
Yeah.

870
01:35:33.293 --> 01:35:36.959
I'm not a student.
I don't have to go.

871
01:35:41.209 --> 01:35:44.451
Well, I'm not a student.
I won't go.

872
01:35:44.543 --> 01:35:46.526
You have to!
The Japanese have counted you!

873
01:35:46.626 --> 01:35:49.568
- I don't care, I won't go!
- You have to go!

874
01:35:49.751 --> 01:35:53.501
Now you're saying you aren't a student.
Why didn't you tell the Japanese earlier?

875
01:35:57.568 --> 01:36:00.751
Stop staring at me!

876
01:36:00.859 --> 01:36:03.084
Save your attitude for the Japanese!

877
01:36:03.801 --> 01:36:06.601
Do you think the Japanese
really invited you to sing?

878
01:36:06.609 --> 01:36:08.068
Dream on!

879
01:36:08.251 --> 01:36:13.526
What do they do all day in Nanking?
They murder, burn, and rape!

880
01:36:13.601 --> 01:36:17.326
You know? Go ahead and go,
but I won't go!

881
01:36:17.418 --> 01:36:19.301
Mosquito, you shut up!

882
01:36:22.209 --> 01:36:25.401
You are all mean to me!
I'm not going!

883
01:36:43.709 --> 01:36:46.259
That's not true what she said.

884
01:36:46.876 --> 01:36:50.034
These men are different from the others.

885
01:36:50.709 --> 01:36:52.684
These men are educated.

886
01:36:52.668 --> 01:36:54.409
They are officers.

887
01:36:54.709 --> 01:36:56.676
These men are gentlemen.

888
01:36:57.876 --> 01:37:01.476
I've been to things like
these before, and...

889
01:37:02.001 --> 01:37:05.418
it's nice. It's elegant. It's a...

890
01:37:05.793 --> 01:37:07.409
It's a party.

891
01:37:07.876 --> 01:37:10.659
There's nice things at parties.
There's cakes and there's flowers

892
01:37:10.668 --> 01:37:12.893
and there's chocolates
and there's dancing and there's...

893
01:37:12.959 --> 01:37:16.018
...all of these things,
which are lovely.

894
01:37:17.276 --> 01:37:19.876
Please don't think about what she said.

895
01:37:22.734 --> 01:37:24.893
I'm a terrible dancer...

896
01:37:25.418 --> 01:37:28.151
...and maybe one day one of you
could teach me how to dance.

897
01:37:28.218 --> 01:37:30.018
That would be nice.

898
01:37:33.084 --> 01:37:35.201
Please don't think about that.

899
01:37:35.459 --> 01:37:37.309
Because that's not true.

900
01:38:02.209 --> 01:38:03.401
I...

901
01:38:05.526 --> 01:38:07.518
...lied to you as well.

902
01:38:07.543 --> 01:38:10.459
Your two friends who went
for the pipa strings...

903
01:38:10.918 --> 01:38:12.626
...they weren't shot.

904
01:38:14.168 --> 01:38:15.576
I'm sorry.

905
01:38:15.668 --> 01:38:17.601
I think you already knew.

906
01:38:18.709 --> 01:38:19.893
Yes.

907
01:38:23.751 --> 01:38:27.926
Sometimes, the truth is the last
thing we need to hear.

908
01:38:41.126 --> 01:38:43.643
I heard what you said to the girls.

909
01:38:44.543 --> 01:38:48.068
- What are you gonna do?
- I gotta get the truck started.

910
01:38:49.376 --> 01:38:50.976
And after that?

911
01:38:54.501 --> 01:38:56.334
I have an idea.

912
01:38:57.084 --> 01:38:59.501
Maybe I can save one of them...

913
01:38:59.693 --> 01:39:02.043
...with your help.
- How?

914
01:39:02.751 --> 01:39:05.601
The Japanese thought
Mosquito was one of the girls.

915
01:39:06.334 --> 01:39:09.218
She tricked them.
Why can't I?

916
01:39:12.334 --> 01:39:13.459
No.

917
01:39:13.568 --> 01:39:16.343
If you're saying
what I think you're saying, no.

918
01:39:16.409 --> 01:39:17.343
No.

919
01:39:18.209 --> 01:39:19.909
That's not happening.

920
01:39:21.401 --> 01:39:25.009
Remember? Like them,
I was at a convent for six years.

921
01:39:28.376 --> 01:39:30.076
But unlike them...

922
01:39:30.334 --> 01:39:32.451
...I was raped by my stepfather

923
01:39:32.518 --> 01:39:34.926
when I was thirteen years old.

924
01:39:39.526 --> 01:39:41.234
By their age...

925
01:39:42.126 --> 01:39:45.801
...I was already forced to
take my first clients.

926
01:39:49.959 --> 01:39:52.209
I don't want them to go through that.

927
01:39:55.251 --> 01:39:57.684
But I can't let you do that, Mo.

928
01:40:00.234 --> 01:40:02.251
I can't let you do that.

929
01:40:13.084 --> 01:40:14.693
What are you doing?

930
01:40:14.818 --> 01:40:16.509
Get back in.

931
01:40:16.668 --> 01:40:18.168
You can't leave.

932
01:40:18.251 --> 01:40:20.218
Get back in!
Get in there!

933
01:40:21.418 --> 01:40:23.118
What are you doing?

934
01:40:23.626 --> 01:40:25.018
Go back!

935
01:40:26.543 --> 01:40:28.376
I said go back in!

936
01:40:59.709 --> 01:41:01.476
I will be the first.

937
01:41:01.526 --> 01:41:03.793
Remember who's in front of you.

938
01:41:04.084 --> 01:41:06.743
When we go,
we will stick to this order.

939
01:41:07.459 --> 01:41:10.059
Shu, isn't there a better solution?

940
01:41:10.526 --> 01:41:11.743
No.

941
01:41:12.543 --> 01:41:15.668
We won't let the Japanese
hurt us again.

942
01:41:46.193 --> 01:41:48.376
Girls. Shu!

943
01:41:48.501 --> 01:41:50.076
Wait, just...

944
01:41:50.584 --> 01:41:53.376
- Go away!
- Come down! Okay, okay.

945
01:41:53.401 --> 01:41:55.168
Stay back, okay.

946
01:41:55.401 --> 01:41:58.093
Don't do anything foolish!
So many people have died.

947
01:41:58.168 --> 01:42:01.368
Even hell is packed.
Why should you add to the crowd?

948
01:42:04.293 --> 01:42:08.084
Shu, don't do this.
You can't do this!

949
01:42:08.259 --> 01:42:10.609
We can't just throw our lives away.

950
01:42:10.668 --> 01:42:12.859
Life is a sacred gift.

951
01:42:12.959 --> 01:42:15.168
It's not ours to throw away.

952
01:42:16.668 --> 01:42:19.693
- Keep away! Step back!
- Okay.

953
01:42:19.876 --> 01:42:22.834
We're stepping back.

954
01:42:24.251 --> 01:42:25.718
Come up!

955
01:42:25.751 --> 01:42:28.309
Didn't we say we are
going to jump together?

956
01:42:28.418 --> 01:42:29.784
Up here!

957
01:42:30.734 --> 01:42:32.301
Come up now!

958
01:42:32.668 --> 01:42:36.776
Listen to me, Shu, I have an idea.
I will go in your place.

959
01:42:38.418 --> 01:42:41.551
Tell the girls to get down.
Tomorrow I will go for you.

960
01:42:41.568 --> 01:42:44.034
Did you hear me?
I will go in your place!

961
01:42:44.168 --> 01:42:46.893
What? Who is going in who's place?

962
01:42:51.543 --> 01:42:52.851
I will also go for you.

963
01:42:52.918 --> 01:42:54.793
Right, we will all go instead of you.
We can handle the Japs.

964
01:42:54.834 --> 01:42:56.734
We will protect you.
We will replace you!

965
01:42:56.834 --> 01:43:00.584
- Don't worry, you have us to protect you.
- Yes, we won't let the Japanese hurt you.

966
01:43:00.626 --> 01:43:03.043
Do you hear us?
We will go in your place.

967
01:43:03.084 --> 01:43:06.593
Come down and don't jump.
Come down.

968
01:43:06.751 --> 01:43:09.743
We're telling them the idea
I told you about.

969
01:43:11.459 --> 01:43:14.326
It's a good idea. That's it, girls.

970
01:43:14.459 --> 01:43:17.451
Shu, come here, it's a good idea.

971
01:43:17.609 --> 01:43:19.559
We can trick the Japanese.

972
01:43:19.584 --> 01:43:21.243
Alright? We'll make it fun.

973
01:43:21.251 --> 01:43:23.351
Come down, we think about it.

974
01:43:23.443 --> 01:43:26.018
Just come down, and think about it.

975
01:43:26.343 --> 01:43:28.284
We can make it work.

976
01:43:35.734 --> 01:43:39.018
We only said it so they would
get down from the tower.

977
01:43:41.751 --> 01:43:44.443
But you shouldn't have lied to them.

978
01:43:44.501 --> 01:43:48.743
Hua, remember? If you weren't lied to,
you wouldn't have ended up in a brothel.

979
01:43:48.793 --> 01:43:51.968
Shut up! Mosquito.
I'm not stupid.

980
01:43:52.026 --> 01:43:56.484
If nobody goes you'll still have to go.
You were counted by the Japanese!

981
01:43:58.859 --> 01:44:01.143
Unless the Japanese are insane,

982
01:44:01.209 --> 01:44:03.476
I don't think they will kill us.

983
01:44:03.526 --> 01:44:05.226
They just want pleasure.

984
01:44:05.459 --> 01:44:09.234
That's what we do.
We have experienced all kinds of men.

985
01:44:09.426 --> 01:44:12.901
As long as we can get out alive,
we will find a way to survive.

986
01:44:13.584 --> 01:44:14.709
Ling,

987
01:44:14.818 --> 01:44:18.059
how do you expect the girls
to handle the Japanese?

988
01:44:18.593 --> 01:44:22.501
Even if they make it back alive,
they won't be able to carry on.

989
01:44:24.459 --> 01:44:28.751
I just don't think it's worth it.
They wouldn't even let us use the bathroom,

990
01:44:28.793 --> 01:44:31.659
yet, we're supposed to kiss their asses,
and sacrifice ourselves for them?

991
01:44:31.734 --> 01:44:34.409
I don't want to hear your nonsense.

992
01:44:34.443 --> 01:44:37.084
If Shu hadn't diverted
the Japs the other day,

993
01:44:37.126 --> 01:44:39.418
where would we all be right now?

994
01:44:43.543 --> 01:44:46.626
Remember how the ancient poem describes us?

995
01:44:48.443 --> 01:44:51.759
- "Prostitutes never care about a falling nation,"
- "they sing and dance while others are dying."

996
01:44:51.818 --> 01:44:55.243
You are not so foolish after all.
I'm impressed.

997
01:44:55.459 --> 01:44:57.601
Mo just taught me those two lines.

998
01:44:57.626 --> 01:45:00.609
Of course we should remember
the poem that criticizes us.

999
01:45:00.709 --> 01:45:04.643
But, I think,
we should do something heroic,

1000
01:45:04.709 --> 01:45:06.759
and change the old way of thinking.

1001
01:45:13.709 --> 01:45:14.943
Mo,

1002
01:45:15.084 --> 01:45:18.676
others say I always follow your lead,

1003
01:45:19.068 --> 01:45:21.101
I say, we share the same life.

1004
01:45:21.168 --> 01:45:22.501
Whatever you say,

1005
01:45:22.584 --> 01:45:25.359
I will go with you.
I will go too.

1006
01:45:27.126 --> 01:45:28.676
Me too.

1007
01:45:29.376 --> 01:45:31.068
Count me in.

1008
01:45:32.726 --> 01:45:33.951
Mo...

1009
01:45:35.026 --> 01:45:37.959
we worked together for three years...

1010
01:45:38.626 --> 01:45:41.201
...and you were always more popular than me.

1011
01:45:41.251 --> 01:45:42.684
I know...

1012
01:45:42.818 --> 01:45:44.884
you always looked down on me...

1013
01:45:44.918 --> 01:45:47.293
...and I never respected you either.

1014
01:45:47.626 --> 01:45:50.351
Well, today I hear you.

1015
01:45:50.959 --> 01:45:54.826
I say we all go,
so we can look after each other.

1016
01:45:55.168 --> 01:45:59.351
Mo, you are right.
People say "whores are heartless."

1017
01:46:00.418 --> 01:46:03.793
So tomorrow, let's do something
honorable with our hearts.

1018
01:46:05.418 --> 01:46:07.159
We will all go.

1019
01:46:11.168 --> 01:46:12.968
If they went...

1020
01:46:13.584 --> 01:46:16.043
...how would the Japanese treat them?

1021
01:46:19.084 --> 01:46:21.709
Will they tear their clothes?

1022
01:46:24.001 --> 01:46:25.693
Will they beat them?

1023
01:46:27.668 --> 01:46:31.501
What if the Japanese rape them?

1024
01:46:31.693 --> 01:46:34.043
Are you kidding? No.

1025
01:46:34.493 --> 01:46:36.393
Have you seen these women?

1026
01:46:36.426 --> 01:46:39.059
Those Japanese don't stand a chance.

1027
01:46:40.568 --> 01:46:43.201
These women,
these women are formidable.

1028
01:46:44.234 --> 01:46:46.226
Brave, exquisite...

1029
01:46:46.943 --> 01:46:48.318
...skillful.

1030
01:46:48.568 --> 01:46:51.926
They've got character,
like nobody I've ever met.

1031
01:46:52.459 --> 01:46:53.668
The Japanese?

1032
01:46:54.693 --> 01:46:56.709
They're amateurs, amateurs.

1033
01:46:57.043 --> 01:46:58.543
These women...

1034
01:46:59.084 --> 01:47:01.176
...they are professionals.

1035
01:47:01.968 --> 01:47:03.318
Father John...

1036
01:47:03.984 --> 01:47:06.201
...what exactly do they do?

1037
01:47:11.193 --> 01:47:12.851
You know, they...

1038
01:47:12.876 --> 01:47:15.501
They love and they hate,
just like all of us.

1039
01:47:15.668 --> 01:47:19.209
Maybe they know more
about it than any of us.

1040
01:47:19.859 --> 01:47:21.659
These women if they...

1041
01:47:21.726 --> 01:47:24.326
...they came face to face
with the devil himself,

1042
01:47:24.418 --> 01:47:26.434
he'd be putty in their hands.

1043
01:47:26.584 --> 01:47:28.743
These idiot? These soldiers?

1044
01:47:30.334 --> 01:47:33.259
You think they're scary?
They're not scary.

1045
01:47:33.501 --> 01:47:35.001
If you think somebody's scary,

1046
01:47:35.151 --> 01:47:36.951
you picture them with their pants
around their ankles,

1047
01:47:36.976 --> 01:47:39.209
sitting on the crapper, alright?

1048
01:47:39.276 --> 01:47:40.634
Picture that.

1049
01:47:41.351 --> 01:47:42.976
Not so scary then.

1050
01:47:44.109 --> 01:47:46.226
These women, and you girls,

1051
01:47:46.568 --> 01:47:51.209
you got a... strength and beauty
that will never die.

1052
01:47:51.609 --> 01:47:53.709
So don't you worry about them.

1053
01:47:54.959 --> 01:47:56.809
Don't worry about them.

1054
01:47:58.043 --> 01:47:59.209
But...

1055
01:47:59.334 --> 01:48:02.793
...but they don't look anything like us.

1056
01:48:03.776 --> 01:48:05.543
How can they go?

1057
01:48:07.709 --> 01:48:09.909
That's where my powers come in.

1058
01:48:10.209 --> 01:48:12.109
I don't do much very well.

1059
01:48:12.151 --> 01:48:15.543
That, that I do well.

1060
01:48:16.376 --> 01:48:18.751
And I'll make them look like your twins.

1061
01:48:20.501 --> 01:48:21.793
You'll see.

1062
01:48:29.001 --> 01:48:30.459
Father John...

1063
01:48:30.626 --> 01:48:32.326
...I was wrong,

1064
01:48:32.668 --> 01:48:34.118
I'm sorry.

1065
01:48:34.709 --> 01:48:37.168
Shu, you don't have to be sorry.

1066
01:48:37.918 --> 01:48:39.501
You don't have to be sorry.

1067
01:48:39.793 --> 01:48:41.751
No, I was wrong.

1068
01:48:42.543 --> 01:48:44.034
What is it?

1069
01:48:44.359 --> 01:48:48.126
From the first day she came here...

1070
01:48:48.668 --> 01:48:50.734
...I felt uncomfortable.

1071
01:48:52.376 --> 01:48:53.809
I thought...

1072
01:48:54.776 --> 01:48:56.484
...she was not good.

1073
01:48:56.576 --> 01:48:58.318
I even thought...

1074
01:48:58.401 --> 01:49:01.959
...both of you were not good.

1075
01:49:02.918 --> 01:49:04.001
That's okay.

1076
01:49:04.168 --> 01:49:06.359
I want to say to her...

1077
01:49:06.543 --> 01:49:07.793
...sorry.

1078
01:49:07.834 --> 01:49:09.668
And say to you...

1079
01:49:10.043 --> 01:49:11.351
...I'm sorry.

1080
01:49:11.626 --> 01:49:13.976
You don't have to say you're sorry.

1081
01:49:17.734 --> 01:49:19.918
You got nothing to be sorry about.

1082
01:49:37.818 --> 01:49:40.526
I had seen many people pray before,

1083
01:49:40.543 --> 01:49:43.559
but that night,
the sight of John's back as he prayed

1084
01:49:43.584 --> 01:49:46.526
would stay with me
for the rest of my life.

1085
01:49:53.301 --> 01:49:55.876
They brought new uniforms.

1086
01:49:59.668 --> 01:50:01.834
Our old uniforms were torn...

1087
01:50:02.234 --> 01:50:04.251
...so I brought you new ones.

1088
01:50:04.334 --> 01:50:07.576
Father Ingleman wanted us
to wear them for Christmas.

1089
01:50:08.126 --> 01:50:11.618
- You don't mind me wearing it?
- The sleeves are short.

1090
01:50:12.001 --> 01:50:13.643
Try it on.

1091
01:50:15.501 --> 01:50:16.968
Big sister.

1092
01:50:21.784 --> 01:50:23.759
I can't button it up for you.

1093
01:50:23.818 --> 01:50:26.226
I'm already skinnier from starvation.

1094
01:50:26.276 --> 01:50:30.201
You are not built like a student,
more like a student's wet nurse!

1095
01:50:35.776 --> 01:50:38.543
I have an idea,
to fool the Japanese,

1096
01:50:38.568 --> 01:50:40.984
let's use the curtains
to make the uniforms fit,

1097
01:50:41.043 --> 01:50:43.543
and tear up the sheets
to wrap our chests.

1098
01:50:43.626 --> 01:50:45.876
So, our boobs won't pop out.

1099
01:52:09.543 --> 01:52:12.693
What're we doing, George?
What're we doing?

1100
01:52:12.751 --> 01:52:16.026
Listen, your God teaches,
everybody's born equal, right?

1101
01:52:16.126 --> 01:52:18.459
So, the women, the girls, which?

1102
01:52:20.418 --> 01:52:22.134
What would you do?

1103
01:52:22.859 --> 01:52:24.293
We must.

1104
01:52:25.293 --> 01:52:27.209
What else we can do?

1105
01:52:34.634 --> 01:52:38.576
He gave me these bracelets
so I would go with him.

1106
01:52:39.584 --> 01:52:42.876
I didn't trust him enough so I didn't.

1107
01:52:44.251 --> 01:52:46.209
I should have.

1108
01:52:47.576 --> 01:52:49.084
I was so stupid.

1109
01:52:49.126 --> 01:52:52.009
You would be even more stupid
wearing them to meet the Japs.

1110
01:52:52.043 --> 01:52:53.676
Leave them here.

1111
01:52:53.759 --> 01:52:55.968
Fine, they are yours now.

1112
01:53:00.109 --> 01:53:03.901
When I was your age,
I had already served countless men.

1113
01:53:04.009 --> 01:53:05.443
Little sister...

1114
01:53:05.651 --> 01:53:07.668
...remember to give this back to me.

1115
01:53:07.751 --> 01:53:10.934
I will use the money
to buy myself out of my contract.

1116
01:53:16.001 --> 01:53:18.084
Big sister, I'm sorry.

1117
01:53:19.634 --> 01:53:22.834
Live a good life for me.

1118
01:53:28.959 --> 01:53:31.134
I don't have any things of value,

1119
01:53:31.193 --> 01:53:34.443
that cat is all I have.
He ran away the other day.

1120
01:53:34.751 --> 01:53:37.043
Little sister, promise me,

1121
01:53:37.126 --> 01:53:39.351
- you will find him.
- Okay.

1122
01:53:50.001 --> 01:53:51.626
Remember Dou?

1123
01:53:51.651 --> 01:53:53.459
She wasn't much taller than you.

1124
01:53:54.251 --> 01:53:56.159
Please take good care of it.

1125
01:53:56.234 --> 01:53:58.126
This is Dou's life.

1126
01:53:59.334 --> 01:54:01.576
She wanted to play
"The Qin Huai View,"

1127
01:54:01.584 --> 01:54:03.784
and for that she was killed.

1128
01:54:06.609 --> 01:54:08.709
The Qin Huai View...

1129
01:54:09.168 --> 01:54:10.951
...is that a beautiful song?

1130
01:54:11.043 --> 01:54:13.551
That's our signature song at Jade Paradise.

1131
01:54:15.551 --> 01:54:19.176
Why don't we sing it for Dou?
It was her dying wish after all.

1132
01:54:19.251 --> 01:54:22.884
Let's sing it for the girls,
so they remember us at our best!

1133
01:54:31.001 --> 01:54:36.251
"I have a story,"

1134
01:54:36.459 --> 01:54:41.251
"and let me put it into song."

1135
01:54:41.609 --> 01:54:46.568
"I hope every one of you"

1136
01:54:46.634 --> 01:54:51.793
"can listen to me patiently."

1137
01:54:51.959 --> 01:54:54.459
"Allow me"

1138
01:54:54.526 --> 01:55:02.209
"to sing the legend of the Qin Huai River,"

1139
01:55:02.376 --> 01:55:07.293
"slowly and passionately,"

1140
01:55:07.584 --> 01:55:13.668
"for each one of you."

1141
01:55:20.651 --> 01:55:25.793
"Ever since the ancient era,"

1142
01:55:25.859 --> 01:55:30.626
"the river has been flowing gracefully."

1143
01:55:31.168 --> 01:55:36.209
"it is the beauty of the South,"

1144
01:55:36.234 --> 01:55:41.376
"the elegance of Nanking."

1145
01:55:41.543 --> 01:55:44.059
"Walk in the famous Zhan Palace,"

1146
01:55:44.126 --> 01:55:51.834
"enjoy the spectacular architecture."

1147
01:55:52.001 --> 01:55:54.268
"Look at the Colony of Cranes"

1148
01:55:54.318 --> 01:55:57.009
"with water rippling all around."

1149
01:55:57.251 --> 01:56:04.676
"What a paradise this is."

1150
01:56:06.876 --> 01:56:08.451
Mo, would...

1151
01:56:10.501 --> 01:56:12.293
You look so sweet.

1152
01:56:17.209 --> 01:56:19.501
Would you mind... lying down?

1153
01:56:21.584 --> 01:56:23.401
I'm just not used to...

1154
01:56:23.918 --> 01:56:27.259
- People who can sit?
- Right, people who can sit.

1155
01:56:28.126 --> 01:56:30.776
- Would you mind?
- I understand, I don't mind.

1156
01:56:40.293 --> 01:56:42.459
So madam, what will it be?

1157
01:56:44.709 --> 01:56:46.343
Fourteen years old?

1158
01:56:47.584 --> 01:56:49.434
How about thirteen?

1159
01:56:53.584 --> 01:56:56.151
Until thirteen I was a good girl.

1160
01:56:56.834 --> 01:56:58.143
Very good.

1161
01:56:58.584 --> 01:56:59.984
Thirteen it is.

1162
01:57:01.084 --> 01:57:03.176
So I'll straighten your hair...

1163
01:57:03.418 --> 01:57:05.201
...cut it in a bob.

1164
01:57:09.126 --> 01:57:10.768
I have an idea.

1165
01:57:12.168 --> 01:57:14.184
I think it'll be beautiful.

1166
01:57:17.334 --> 01:57:19.159
This is what we need.

1167
01:57:19.734 --> 01:57:21.151
It's perfect.

1168
01:57:35.043 --> 01:57:37.009
The way you are now...

1169
01:57:38.126 --> 01:57:40.243
...is what I like the best.

1170
01:57:42.693 --> 01:57:44.268
I see you.

1171
01:57:46.126 --> 01:57:48.759
I see everything that you've been through.

1172
01:57:51.168 --> 01:57:53.493
And I want all of that, Mo.

1173
01:57:54.459 --> 01:57:55.334
I want all of it.

1174
01:57:57.359 --> 01:57:58.826
I love it.

1175
01:57:58.926 --> 01:58:00.701
I love it all.

1176
01:58:03.693 --> 01:58:05.984
Are you going to fall in love with me?

1177
01:58:08.293 --> 01:58:10.118
I already have.

1178
01:58:37.818 --> 01:58:39.668
I can do this.

1179
01:58:42.276 --> 01:58:44.659
Sorry, these are not my clothes.

1180
01:58:51.376 --> 01:58:53.201
I wanna promise you something.

1181
01:58:55.443 --> 01:58:57.601
When this war is over,

1182
01:58:57.793 --> 01:58:59.659
I'm gonna find you...

1183
01:59:01.968 --> 01:59:04.176
...and I'm gonna take you home.

1184
01:59:07.209 --> 01:59:08.451
No.

1185
01:59:09.876 --> 01:59:11.534
After tonight...

1186
01:59:12.834 --> 01:59:15.876
...my body will no longer be mine.

1187
01:59:21.251 --> 01:59:23.101
Take me home now.

1188
01:59:59.551 --> 02:00:00.934
Wow, Mo!

1189
02:00:01.001 --> 02:00:03.951
He can turn back time.
He chopped away 5 or 6 years!

1190
02:00:04.001 --> 02:00:08.084
Three more chops and we'd all be infants,
so we can start our lives over again!

1191
02:00:08.168 --> 02:00:11.134
Have you asked him,
where he learned such skills?

1192
02:00:11.593 --> 02:00:14.818
Mo, ask him to cut our hair too.

1193
02:00:15.609 --> 02:00:18.559
They all want you
to give them a makeover.

1194
02:00:19.026 --> 02:00:20.484
My pleasure.

1195
02:00:20.559 --> 02:00:22.626
Glad to serve you.

1196
02:00:32.026 --> 02:00:35.109
- Here?
- He has to work with you lying down.

1197
02:00:35.918 --> 02:00:40.009
Right, he's a mortician,
he only knows how to work on dead people.

1198
02:00:40.126 --> 02:00:41.918
Are they disturbed...

1199
02:00:42.501 --> 02:00:44.193
...by the way I work? Sorry.

1200
02:00:45.793 --> 02:00:47.826
He hopes you won't mind.

1201
02:00:48.334 --> 02:00:50.101
Whatever, who cares?

1202
02:00:50.168 --> 02:00:52.901
I just want to look like
a pretty schoolgirl.

1203
02:00:53.026 --> 02:00:54.709
Give me a coat.

1204
02:01:06.526 --> 02:01:08.368
His hands are so soft.

1205
02:01:08.418 --> 02:01:10.768
Mo, did he really work on the dead?

1206
02:01:10.818 --> 02:01:14.543
Mo, we're going to sleep.
Wake us up when it's our turn.

1207
02:01:27.459 --> 02:01:29.843
You've done this your whole life?

1208
02:01:30.009 --> 02:01:31.626
For five years.

1209
02:01:31.876 --> 02:01:33.951
You do this very well.

1210
02:01:38.484 --> 02:01:39.876
It matters.

1211
02:01:40.709 --> 02:01:42.476
It matters to me.

1212
02:01:44.709 --> 02:01:46.701
Before my daughter died...

1213
02:01:49.876 --> 02:01:51.684
she made me promise...

1214
02:01:52.543 --> 02:01:54.718
...to make her beautiful again.

1215
02:01:56.709 --> 02:01:58.659
That was the first time.

1216
02:02:00.751 --> 02:02:02.184
It's important.

1217
02:02:04.584 --> 02:02:06.084
It's important work.

1218
02:02:07.251 --> 02:02:08.484
I'm sorry.

1219
02:02:10.376 --> 02:02:12.451
She would have been twelve.

1220
02:02:14.793 --> 02:02:16.409
Like the girls.

1221
02:02:17.084 --> 02:02:18.184
Yeah.

1222
02:02:47.626 --> 02:02:49.501
Mo, he's amazing!

1223
02:02:51.209 --> 02:02:54.018
If only my mother were alive,
she would have been so happy

1224
02:02:54.043 --> 02:02:56.109
to see me like this.

1225
02:02:56.126 --> 02:02:59.759
She said,
we never had a scholar in our family.

1226
02:03:03.084 --> 02:03:05.293
Now you are a scholar, so am I.

1227
02:03:05.359 --> 02:03:09.034
- My mother wouldn't recognize me either!
- Of course not.

1228
02:03:09.101 --> 02:03:11.426
We are now students.
Let's line up.

1229
02:03:11.759 --> 02:03:14.701
Mo, let him see
if we all look like students.

1230
02:03:20.193 --> 02:03:22.493
No need to count, we only have twelve.

1231
02:03:23.668 --> 02:03:25.468
We are one short.

1232
02:03:28.001 --> 02:03:30.284
How many did the Japanese say?

1233
02:03:32.543 --> 02:03:33.893
How many?

1234
02:03:35.384 --> 02:03:37.376
- Thirteen.
- How many?

1235
02:03:37.751 --> 02:03:40.668
Thirteen. We only have twelve here.

1236
02:03:42.084 --> 02:03:43.759
This is a terrible joke.

1237
02:03:45.234 --> 02:03:48.626
- One of the students still has to go!
- We did all of this for nothing!

1238
02:03:53.793 --> 02:03:55.326
I will go.

1239
02:03:57.126 --> 02:03:59.368
- What did he say?
- I will go.

1240
02:03:59.834 --> 02:04:01.101
George.

1241
02:04:01.209 --> 02:04:04.376
- He said he would go.
- What are you talking about?

1242
02:04:05.143 --> 02:04:06.818
You are a boy!

1243
02:04:12.043 --> 02:04:15.776
Father Ingleman ask me to protect students.

1244
02:04:16.134 --> 02:04:17.951
But I'm not good.

1245
02:04:18.084 --> 02:04:19.684
I'm... I'm terrible.

1246
02:04:20.209 --> 02:04:23.493
- I'm... I'm bad.
- Who cares if we are one short?

1247
02:04:23.543 --> 02:04:25.976
We will just say that
one of us has died from an illness.

1248
02:04:26.043 --> 02:04:28.768
My grandma told me that
the Japanese can't count.

1249
02:04:29.109 --> 02:04:31.843
We can't do that!
The Japanese are very astute!

1250
02:04:31.943 --> 02:04:35.476
They will search everywhere,
and it will be the end for the students!

1251
02:04:35.526 --> 02:04:38.384
There is nothing you can do.
They will see that you are a boy.

1252
02:04:38.459 --> 02:04:40.176
You can't fool them.

1253
02:04:40.209 --> 02:04:42.184
Yes, it's too obvious.

1254
02:04:42.293 --> 02:04:44.409
It's a short distance
from the church to the car.

1255
02:04:44.459 --> 02:04:48.993
If I am made-up as a girl, lower my head,
and walk right behind you all,

1256
02:04:49.001 --> 02:04:51.451
I'm sure the Japanese won't notice!

1257
02:04:51.884 --> 02:04:55.351
If we have one missing,
the Japanese will find out,

1258
02:04:55.376 --> 02:04:57.334
then... a big trouble.

1259
02:04:57.793 --> 02:05:00.268
You are good at make-up.

1260
02:05:00.334 --> 02:05:03.601
- You can do for me.
- George, I'm not that good.

1261
02:05:03.668 --> 02:05:05.793
No, no, you can.

1262
02:05:06.043 --> 02:05:07.476
George, stop it.

1263
02:05:07.543 --> 02:05:09.209
- It can't work.
- You can!

1264
02:05:11.051 --> 02:05:13.101
The church to the car,

1265
02:05:13.168 --> 02:05:14.818
just a short way!

1266
02:05:14.918 --> 02:05:17.959
You are good at make-up,
you can do for me!

1267
02:05:18.293 --> 02:05:20.251
I will lower my head!

1268
02:05:20.834 --> 02:05:23.793
It's possible, it just a short way!

1269
02:05:27.709 --> 02:05:30.201
You can. It's possible.

1270
02:06:38.126 --> 02:06:40.376
You know what could happen?

1271
02:06:41.209 --> 02:06:43.234
Yes, yes, I know.

1272
02:06:44.168 --> 02:06:47.634
I can do what Father Ingleman tell me.

1273
02:06:49.668 --> 02:06:50.876
Amazing.

1274
02:06:52.043 --> 02:06:55.468
I think I hear
what the Father is saying right now.

1275
02:06:55.751 --> 02:06:57.634
- Yes?
- Yeah.

1276
02:06:58.043 --> 02:07:01.209
- What he saying?
- I think he's saying...

1277
02:07:02.234 --> 02:07:04.551
that you've done an incredible...

1278
02:07:04.668 --> 02:07:08.676
...an incredible job,
taking care of the girls.

1279
02:07:08.876 --> 02:07:11.501
And that you're good, so good.

1280
02:07:13.709 --> 02:07:16.384
And I think he's also asking...

1281
02:07:18.043 --> 02:07:20.434
...what the hell are you doing

1282
02:07:20.501 --> 02:07:23.418
with that awful wig on your head?

1283
02:07:44.526 --> 02:07:47.484
This was the last time I saw George Chen.

1284
02:07:47.584 --> 02:07:50.243
When he was six years old,

1285
02:07:50.301 --> 02:07:53.834
and almost died of starvation,
Father Ingleman saved him.

1286
02:07:54.009 --> 02:07:58.334
He rang the church bell, swept the floor,
and worked in the kitchen.

1287
02:07:58.418 --> 02:08:03.818
We used to laugh at him,
when he spoke in English or Nanking dialect.

1288
02:08:16.459 --> 02:08:18.234
You know that...

1289
02:08:18.509 --> 02:08:20.468
...you can't really go there.

1290
02:08:20.876 --> 02:08:24.251
You gotta escape somehow
before you get there.

1291
02:08:24.293 --> 02:08:27.834
You gotta jump from the car
or the truck or whatever.

1292
02:08:28.501 --> 02:08:31.093
You wait until it slows down,
goes around the corner,

1293
02:08:31.168 --> 02:08:34.568
- that's when you jump.
- No, I'm no jumping.

1294
02:08:34.668 --> 02:08:36.559
- Don't teach me.
- Why not?

1295
02:08:36.918 --> 02:08:38.534
If I jump...

1296
02:08:39.293 --> 02:08:41.468
...Japanese will find out.

1297
02:08:42.001 --> 02:08:45.609
I will go all the way,
give you more time.

1298
02:08:46.193 --> 02:08:48.126
You and the girls...

1299
02:08:48.793 --> 02:08:50.776
...get out of the church.

1300
02:09:05.918 --> 02:09:07.851
Hide your weapons well.
Don't let the Japanese see.

1301
02:09:08.026 --> 02:09:11.068
Don't worry,
at least we will get an eyeball.

1302
02:09:21.109 --> 02:09:23.368
Have you got something as well?

1303
02:09:58.943 --> 02:10:01.601
Following our commander's order,

1304
02:10:01.751 --> 02:10:04.059
I'm here to pick up the students.

1305
02:10:07.193 --> 02:10:09.984
Here is a gift bag from our troops.

1306
02:10:10.084 --> 02:10:11.809
Please accept it.

1307
02:10:34.743 --> 02:10:36.326
What are you doing here?

1308
02:10:37.051 --> 02:10:38.443
Mr Kato...

1309
02:10:39.193 --> 02:10:42.501
...have you spoken with Colonel Hasegawa?

1310
02:10:42.943 --> 02:10:44.368
My daughter,

1311
02:10:44.418 --> 02:10:47.351
she doesn't have to go, right?

1312
02:10:47.901 --> 02:10:52.018
The order is from the chief commander.
Even Colonel Hasegawa can't interfere.

1313
02:10:52.376 --> 02:10:53.851
Get out.

1314
02:10:53.959 --> 02:10:56.668
Mr Kato,
but you promised to help.

1315
02:10:56.751 --> 02:10:58.018
Shut up!

1316
02:10:59.251 --> 02:11:01.426
The chief commander is in charge.

1317
02:11:01.459 --> 02:11:02.601
Look...

1318
02:11:02.834 --> 02:11:04.626
...he sent troops just for this.

1319
02:11:04.709 --> 02:11:06.451
We can't do anything.

1320
02:11:07.793 --> 02:11:09.834
But we had a deal.

1321
02:11:10.109 --> 02:11:13.459
I have given you all of my valuables.

1322
02:11:13.834 --> 02:11:16.701
Mr Kato, please, you promised!

1323
02:11:16.793 --> 02:11:19.293
When did I take your things?

1324
02:11:23.293 --> 02:11:25.959
That was for our military expenses.

1325
02:11:30.626 --> 02:11:34.209
Then I'm begging you,
please allow me to see

1326
02:11:34.293 --> 02:11:36.359
my daughter one last time.

1327
02:13:18.093 --> 02:13:20.918
I'm not a student. I won't go!

1328
02:13:21.084 --> 02:13:23.001
I won't go!

1329
02:13:23.276 --> 02:13:25.093
I'm not a student!

1330
02:13:26.818 --> 02:13:29.551
Isn't that your daughter?
What is she saying?

1331
02:13:29.651 --> 02:13:31.434
Why is she shouting?

1332
02:13:31.543 --> 02:13:35.543
I'm not a student!

1333
02:13:40.209 --> 02:13:42.793
I won't go!

1334
02:13:50.651 --> 02:13:52.743
Be gentle with her, she's just a girl.

1335
02:14:06.884 --> 02:14:08.926
You've seen your daughter.

1336
02:14:59.468 --> 02:15:01.368
Let's go. Come on.

1337
02:15:19.918 --> 02:15:21.143
Shu.

1338
02:15:21.876 --> 02:15:23.326
Come here.

1339
02:15:25.193 --> 02:15:27.834
Your father is a good man.

1340
02:15:27.943 --> 02:15:30.376
We could never have done this,
without your father.

1341
02:15:30.459 --> 02:15:32.118
He's a good man.

1342
02:15:37.959 --> 02:15:39.518
Watch your legs.

1343
02:17:25.709 --> 02:17:30.326
John told me, his biggest regret was
as we had to get out as quickly as possible,

1344
02:17:30.376 --> 02:17:32.934
he couldn't give my father a proper burial.

1345
02:18:01.826 --> 02:18:05.543
Is this good for me to go through?

1346
02:18:08.834 --> 02:18:10.593
What's on the truck?

1347
02:18:14.543 --> 02:18:16.226
Empty wine cases, but...

1348
02:18:16.609 --> 02:18:20.193
four of them are full. They are...
very good, very good.

1349
02:18:20.293 --> 02:18:21.476
Here.

1350
02:18:21.609 --> 02:18:23.501
You see, vintage.

1351
02:18:24.443 --> 02:18:26.201
If you would like some.

1352
02:18:27.001 --> 02:18:28.351
Open it.

1353
02:18:33.726 --> 02:18:34.993
These.

1354
02:18:35.709 --> 02:18:36.809
Take.

1355
02:19:18.151 --> 02:19:19.743
Until this day

1356
02:19:19.751 --> 02:19:23.568
I still don't know what happened
to the women of the Qin Huai River.

1357
02:19:23.626 --> 02:19:26.618
I never learned all of their names,

1358
02:19:26.651 --> 02:19:30.043
and never saw them
being taken away by the Japanese.

1359
02:19:30.084 --> 02:19:32.176
So, I always imagine...

1360
02:19:32.418 --> 02:19:35.051
I imagine myself standing
by the large round window,

1361
02:19:35.109 --> 02:19:37.426
watching them walk in once again.
